From b1cc244a0c7b636f4a4c41363751bae1e2abed13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 19:48:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] feat(wallpaper): add Bing as a 5th browsable source in
 the OCS browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the Bing Image of the Day feed as a fifth pseudo-provider in the
OCS wallpaper browser, alongside pling/opendesktop/kde-look/gnome-look.
Bing already lives in a persistent, already-a-Wallpaper-Source archive
(/var/cache/ncz-wallpapers/bing/<market>) with its own
retention-and-pin mechanism, so the per-item action is PIN, not
import -- importing would copy a file that already exists on disk and
misattribute a Bing photo into a pack named for OCS (operator decision,
recorded here as the explicit reason this branch never builds an
import/copy path for Bing).

Core model (src/core/wallpaper_ocs.vala):

- New WallpaperBing class with two static parsers:
    * markets(string) -> ArrayList<WallpaperOcsChoice>
      Parses the TSV from `ncz-wallpaper-bing markets` -- one
      "<market>\t<name>" per line. Tolerates blank lines and
      comment-shaped lines without a tab. Sorts by display name.
    * items(string)   -> ArrayList<WallpaperOcsItem>
      Parses the bare JSON array from `ncz-wallpaper-bing list <market>`
      (no schema/items wrapper, unlike OCS). Each element maps onto the
      shared WallpaperOcsItem shape with the new Bing-only fields
      populated. Rejects non-array roots, bad provider ids, and missing
      or non-bool pinned fields.

- WallpaperOcsItem extended with three additive, defaulted fields
  (thumbnail_path, pinned, market) so the Bing item type does not need
  to be a parallel class. add_card / filter_cards / card_matches /
  thumbnails all already operate on WallpaperOcsItem, so a second type
  would mean duplicated rendering or a parallel grid -- not justified
  for an additive provider. The key stays provider-namespaced via the
  existing provider + id formula.

- WallpaperOcs.providers() / categories() / items() are unchanged --
  Bing parsing lives entirely in WallpaperBing, keeping the OCS parsers
  strictly about OCS JSON.

Browser (src/components/sidebar/pages/wallpaper_ocs_browser.vala):

- initialize() appends a synthetic WallpaperOcsChoice("bing", "Bing")
  to the SelectionRow AFTER the real provider list. The SelectionRow
  shows the display name "Bing" but stores the id "bing" so
  select_provider(id) keeps working.

- select_provider("bing") routes to a new select_provider_bing() that
  runs `ncz-wallpaper-bing markets` and feeds the TSV through
  WallpaperBing.markets(). The same chip row, the same filter state,
  the same browse_all() flow -- the only difference is which command
  produced the choices.

- worker() branches on state.provider. For Bing the per-unit command
  is `ncz-wallpaper-bing list <market>` (one call returns everything
  archived for that market, no --pages / pagination concept; the
  existing retention window already bounds it). CRAWL_CATEGORY_TIMEOUT
  still applies. The bounded worker pool, item cap, and cancellation
  machinery carry over unchanged.

- thumbnails() branches on card.item.thumbnail_path: for Bing it loads
  a local file directly via File.read_async + Gdk.Pixbuf.from_stream_
  at_scale_async + synchronous stream.close() (Vala forbids yields
  inside a finally block, so close is inlined after the load and on
  the error path). For OCS the existing Soup path is untouched.

- add_card() branches the action button: Bing gets a Pin/Pinned toggle
  that calls `ncz-wallpaper-bing pin|unpin <market> <yyyymmdd>` and
  flips its own label on success. No WallpaperOcsImports involvement
  at all -- that class is specifically about the imported-ocs sidecar
  pack and does not apply here. Real OCS providers keep the existing
  Import/Added/Retry-import flow exactly as it is. The attribution
  line shows "bing · <market>" for Bing items (the existing
  "Unknown uploader · bing" fallback read badly for an automated
  Bing feed).

- New pin_card(OcsCard card) async method next to import_card. Splits
  the composite id ("<market>:<date>") back into (market, date) and
  argv that to the helper. Uses a fresh Cancellable (null) and a 15s
  budget so a pending browse-all cancellation cannot kill the user's
  explicit pin click.

Tests (tests/wallpaper_ocs_test.vala):

Seven new test functions exercise the WallpaperBing parsers against
realistic fixtures (the documented `ncz-wallpaper-bing` TSV and JSON
shapes, including an item with pinned:true and one with pinned:false,
plus all the rejection cases for malformed input):

- /ocs/bing-markets-parses-tsv
- /ocs/bing-markets-tolerates-blank-lines-and-whitespace
- /ocs/bing-markets-empty
- /ocs/bing-items-parses-list-array
- /ocs/bing-items-empty-array
- /ocs/bing-items-rejects-non-array-root
- /ocs/bing-items-rejects-bad-pinned-field

Verified: full container build of singularity-opt.tgz on ULTRA
(debian:forky arm64, podman) stages successfully. `strings` on the
staged singularity-desktop ELF confirms the new symbols (WallpaperBing
class, pin_card, select_provider_bing) and UI strings ("Bing",
"Pinned", "Pinning Bing image", etc.) are present. `meson test
-C build wallpaper-ocs` reports all 21 tests OK (the 14 pre-existing
OCS tests plus the 7 new Bing tests). Real `ncz-wallpaper-bing`
binary was NOT exercised -- it is not installed in the build container
or on ULTRA, so verification is against the documented JSON/TSV
shapes only.
